IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`
IMPORT `dg2-indemnification`

-- Tests of dg2-indemnification.l4 (8 Del. C. section 145). Expected values are written by hand from src:435 to src:455 of
-- de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, beside each assertion, before the run.

§ `Section 145(a)`

-- (a party to a proceeding, the proceeding is by or in the right of the corporation, by reason of the person's capacity, the kind of amount,
-- actually and reasonably incurred, good faith, reasonable belief, the proceeding is criminal, no reasonable cause to believe the conduct unlawful)
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A `s 145 Kind of amount`
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 145(a) Facts`
`a third-party claim` a b c d e f g h i MEANS `s 145(a) Facts` WITH
    `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action, suit or proceeding, whether civil, criminal, administrative or investigative` IS a
    `the action, suit or proceeding is one by or in the right of the corporation` IS b
    `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise` IS c
    `the kind of amount` IS d
    `the amount was actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the action, suit or proceeding` IS e
    `the person acted in good faith` IS f
    `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` IS g
    `the action or proceeding is criminal` IS h
    `the person had no reasonable cause to believe the person's conduct was unlawful` IS i

#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `expenses (including attorneys' fees)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `judgments` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `fines` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `amounts paid in settlement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An amount of another kind is not in the four the text names.
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `an amount of any other kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An action by or in the right of the corporation is for (b).
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `expenses (including attorneys' fees)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Each condition is required.
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` FALSE FALSE TRUE `expenses (including attorneys' fees)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE `expenses (including attorneys' fees)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `expenses (including attorneys' fees)` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `expenses (including attorneys' fees)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `expenses (including attorneys' fees)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- In a criminal proceeding the person must also have had no reasonable cause to believe the conduct unlawful; in a civil one that is not asked.
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `fines` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against the amount` (`a third-party claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `fines` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- src:436: termination by judgment, order, settlement, conviction or nolo plea creates no presumption of itself.
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the way the proceeding ended of itself creates a presumption that the person did not act in good faith` `by judgment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the way the proceeding ended of itself creates a presumption that the person did not act in good faith` `by order` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the way the proceeding ended of itself creates a presumption that the person did not act in good faith` `by settlement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the way the proceeding ended of itself creates a presumption that the person did not act in good faith` `by conviction` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the way the proceeding ended of itself creates a presumption that the person did not act in good faith` `upon a plea of nolo contendere or its equivalent` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(a) the way the proceeding ended of itself creates a presumption that the person did not act in good faith` `in any other way` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 145(b)`

-- (a party to an action by or in the right of the corporation, by reason of capacity, expenses, good faith, reasonable belief, adjudged liable,
-- the court has determined the person fairly and reasonably entitled, the expenses the court deems proper)
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A NUMBER
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 145(b) Facts`
`a derivative claim` a b c d e f g h MEANS `s 145(b) Facts` WITH
    `the person was or is a party, or is threatened to be made a party, to a threatened, pending or completed action or suit by or in the right of the corporation to procure a judgment in its favor` IS a
    `the person is a party or threatened by reason of the fact that the person is or was a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation, or is or was serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another corporation, partnership, joint venture, trust or other enterprise` IS b
    `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense or settlement of the action or suit` IS c
    `the person acted in good faith` IS d
    `the person acted in a manner the person reasonably believed to be in or not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` IS e
    `the person has been adjudged to be liable to the corporation in respect of the claim, issue or matter` IS f
    `the Court of Chancery or the court in which the action or suit was brought has determined upon application that, despite the adjudication of liability but in view of all the circumstances, the person is fairly and reasonably entitled to indemnity for expenses` IS g
    `the expenses the court has deemed proper` IS h

#ASSERT `s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `s 145(b) the most the corporation has power to indemnify against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) EQUALS 1000
-- Adjudged liable to the corporation: nothing unless and only to the extent the court so determines.
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `s 145(b) the most the corporation has power to indemnify against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 400)
#ASSERT `s 145(b) the most the corporation has power to indemnify against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 400) EQUALS 400
-- The court cannot allow more than the expenses incurred.
#ASSERT `s 145(b) the most the corporation has power to indemnify against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1500) EQUALS 1000
-- Good faith and the reasonable belief are each required; so are the capacity and the party status.
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` (`a derivative claim` FALSE TRUE 1000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(b) the corporation has power to indemnify the person against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE FALSE 1000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `s 145(b) the most the corporation has power to indemnify against expenses` (`a derivative claim` TRUE TRUE 1000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0) EQUALS 0

§ `Section 145(c)`

-- (a present or former director, a present or former officer, the date of the act or omission, deemed to have consented to service under
-- 10 Del. C. section 3114(b), successful on the merits or otherwise, the expenses actually and reasonably incurred)
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A DATE
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 145(c) Facts`
`a success` a b c d e f MEANS `s 145(c) Facts` WITH
    `the person is a present or former director of the corporation` IS a
    `the person is a present or former officer of the corporation` IS b
    `the date of the act or omission` IS c
    `at the time of the act or omission the person is deemed to have consented to service by the delivery of process to the registered agent of the corporation pursuant to 10 Del. C. section 3114(b)` IS d
    `the person has been successful on the merits or otherwise in defense of the action, suit or proceeding referred to in subsections (a) and (b), or of a claim, issue or matter therein` IS e
    `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) actually and reasonably incurred by the person in connection with the defense` IS f

-- (c)(1): a successful present or former director or officer shall be indemnified against the expenses.
#ASSERT `s 145(c)(1) the person must be indemnified against the expenses` (`a success` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) FALSE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT `s 145(c)(1) the expenses the person must be indemnified against` (`a success` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) FALSE TRUE 800) EQUALS 800
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(c)(1) the person must be indemnified against the expenses` (`a success` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) FALSE FALSE 800)
#ASSERT `s 145(c)(1) the expenses the person must be indemnified against` (`a success` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) FALSE FALSE 800) EQUALS 0
-- "officer": for an act on or before 31 December 2020 any officer; after that date only an officer deemed to have consented to service.
#ASSERT `s 145(c)(1) the person must be indemnified against the expenses` (`a success` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 12 31) FALSE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(c)(1) the person must be indemnified against the expenses` (`a success` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) FALSE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT `s 145(c)(1) the person must be indemnified against the expenses` (`a success` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) TRUE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT `s 145(c) the person is an officer for the purposes of paragraphs (c)(1) and (c)(2)` (`a success` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 12 31) FALSE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(c) the person is an officer for the purposes of paragraphs (c)(1) and (c)(2)` (`a success` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) FALSE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(c) the person is an officer for the purposes of paragraphs (c)(1) and (c)(2)` (`a success` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) TRUE TRUE 800)
-- (c)(2): the corporation may indemnify any other person (not a director or officer in that sense) to the extent successful.
#ASSERT `s 145(c)(2) the corporation may indemnify the person against the expenses` (`a success` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) FALSE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT `s 145(c)(2) the corporation may indemnify the person against the expenses` (`a success` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) FALSE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(c)(2) the corporation may indemnify the person against the expenses` (`a success` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) TRUE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(c)(2) the corporation may indemnify the person against the expenses` (`a success` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) FALSE TRUE 800)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(c)(2) the corporation may indemnify the person against the expenses` (`a success` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2024 1 1) FALSE FALSE 800)

§ `Section 145(d)`

-- (ordered by a court, the person is a director or officer at the time, the determination was made in the specific case, it found the standard
-- met, who made it, the committee was designated by majority vote, there are no non-party directors, the non-party directors directed counsel)
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A `s 145(d) Who made the determination`
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 145(d) Facts`
`a determination` a b c d e f g h MEANS `s 145(d) Facts` WITH
    `the indemnification is ordered by a court` IS a
    `the person is a director or officer of the corporation at the time of the determination` IS b
    `the determination was made as authorized in the specific case` IS c
    `the determination is that the person has met the applicable standard of conduct set forth in subsections (a) and (b)` IS d
    `who made the determination` IS e
    `the committee was designated by majority vote of the directors who are not parties` IS f
    `there are no directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding` IS g
    `the directors who are not parties directed that independent legal counsel make the determination` IS h

#ASSERT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `someone else` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a majority vote of the directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding, even though less than a quorum` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `a majority vote of the directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding, even though less than a quorum` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `a majority vote of the directors who are not parties to the action, suit or proceeding, even though less than a quorum` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a committee of such directors designated by majority vote of such directors, even though less than a quorum` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `a committee of such directors designated by majority vote of such directors, even though less than a quorum` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Independent legal counsel: only if there are no such directors, or such directors so direct.
#ASSERT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `independent legal counsel in a written opinion` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `independent legal counsel in a written opinion` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `independent legal counsel in a written opinion` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `the stockholders` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE `someone else` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- A person who is not a director or officer at the time: the text prescribes no method, so a determination in the specific case suffices.
#ASSERT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `someone else` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(d) the indemnification under subsection (a) or (b) may be made` (`a determination` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `someone else` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 145(e)`

-- (a present officer or director, a former director or officer or another employee or agent, incurred in defending a proceeding, an undertaking received)
#ASSERT `s 145(e) the corporation may pay the expenses in advance of the final disposition` (`s 145(e) Facts` WITH `the person is a present officer or director of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` IS FALSE, `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) were incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding` IS TRUE, `the corporation has received an undertaking by or on behalf of the director or officer to repay the amount if it shall ultimately be determined that the person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(e) the corporation may pay the expenses in advance of the final disposition` (`s 145(e) Facts` WITH `the person is a present officer or director of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` IS FALSE, `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) were incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding` IS TRUE, `the corporation has received an undertaking by or on behalf of the director or officer to repay the amount if it shall ultimately be determined that the person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Former directors and officers, other employees and agents: on such terms as the corporation deems appropriate; no undertaking is required by the text.
#ASSERT `s 145(e) the corporation may pay the expenses in advance of the final disposition` (`s 145(e) Facts` WITH `the person is a present officer or director of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` IS TRUE, `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) were incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding` IS TRUE, `the corporation has received an undertaking by or on behalf of the director or officer to repay the amount if it shall ultimately be determined that the person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Expenses not incurred in defending a proceeding, or a person of none of the kinds: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 145(e) the corporation may pay the expenses in advance of the final disposition` (`s 145(e) Facts` WITH `the person is a present officer or director of the corporation` IS TRUE, `the person is a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` IS FALSE, `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) were incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding` IS FALSE, `the corporation has received an undertaking by or on behalf of the director or officer to repay the amount if it shall ultimately be determined that the person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145(e) the corporation may pay the expenses in advance of the final disposition` (`s 145(e) Facts` WITH `the person is a present officer or director of the corporation` IS FALSE, `the person is a former director or officer, or another employee or agent of the corporation, or a person serving at the request of the corporation as a director, officer, employee or agent of another enterprise` IS FALSE, `the expenses (including attorneys' fees) were incurred in defending a civil, criminal, administrative or investigative action, suit or proceeding` IS TRUE, `the corporation has received an undertaking by or on behalf of the director or officer to repay the amount if it shall ultimately be determined that the person is not entitled to be indemnified by the corporation as authorized in this section` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 145(f), (j), (k)`

#ASSERT NOT `s 145(f) the other subsections of this section are the exclusive source of the person's rights` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(f) the other subsections of this section are the exclusive source of the person's rights` FALSE
-- (f) second sentence: a right under the certificate or a bylaw is not cut off by an amendment after the act or omission, unless the provision in effect explicitly allows it.
#ASSERT `s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `in the certificate of incorporation` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `in the bylaws` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `in the bylaws` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `in the bylaws` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `in the bylaws` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `in the bylaws` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 2) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(f) the right is protected from elimination or impairment by the later amendment, repeal or elimination` `in a resolution of the board of directors` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1) FALSE
-- (j): unless otherwise provided when authorized or ratified, the right continues after the person ceases to be a director etc. and passes to heirs, executors and administrators.
#ASSERT `s 145(j) the indemnification and advancement continue as to a person who has ceased to be a director, officer, employee or agent` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(j) the indemnification and advancement continue as to a person who has ceased to be a director, officer, employee or agent` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(j) the indemnification and advancement inure to the benefit of the heirs, executors and administrators of the person` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(j) the indemnification and advancement inure to the benefit of the heirs, executors and administrators of the person` TRUE
-- (k): the Court of Chancery has exclusive jurisdiction over actions for advancement or indemnification, and may summarily determine the obligation to advance.
#ASSERT `s 145(k) the Court of Chancery has exclusive jurisdiction over the action` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(k) the Court of Chancery has exclusive jurisdiction over the action` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145(k) the Court of Chancery may summarily determine the question` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(k) the Court of Chancery may summarily determine the question` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 145(g), (h), (i)`

#ASSERT `s 145(g) the corporation has power to purchase and maintain insurance on behalf of the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(g) the corporation has power to purchase and maintain insurance on behalf of the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(g) the corporation has power to purchase and maintain insurance on behalf of the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (insurance provided through a captive insurance company, the captive is organized and licensed, term (g)(1), term (g)(2), term (g)(3))
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 145(g) Facts about insurance through a captive insurance company`
`a captive` a b c d e MEANS `s 145(g) Facts about insurance through a captive insurance company` WITH
    `the insurance is provided directly or indirectly by or through a captive insurance company` IS a
    `the captive insurance company is organized and licensed in compliance with the laws of a jurisdiction` IS b
    `the terms exclude coverage for, and provide that the insurer shall not pay, loss arising out of a personal profit or financial advantage to which the person was not legally entitled, or a deliberate criminal or deliberate fraudulent act or a knowing violation of law, if established by a final, nonappealable adjudication in the underlying proceeding (not an action or proceeding to determine coverage), unless and only to the extent the person is entitled to be indemnified under this section` IS c
    `the terms require that a determination to make a payment in respect of a claim against a current director or officer be made by an independent claims administrator or in accordance with paragraphs (d)(1) through (4)` IS d
    `the terms require that, before a payment in connection with a dismissal or compromise of an action, suit or proceeding by or in the right of the corporation as to which notice is required to be given to stockholders, the corporation include in the notice that a payment is proposed to be made under the insurance` IS e

#ASSERT `s 145(g) the insurance is insurance for the purposes of this subsection` (`a captive` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 145(g) the insurance is insurance for the purposes of this subsection` (`a captive` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(g) the insurance is insurance for the purposes of this subsection` (`a captive` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(g) the insurance is insurance for the purposes of this subsection` (`a captive` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(g) the insurance is insurance for the purposes of this subsection` (`a captive` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(g) the insurance is insurance for the purposes of this subsection` (`a captive` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(g) the conduct of an insured person is imputed to another insured person for the purposes of paragraph (g)(1)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 145(g) the corporation is, solely by virtue of the captive insurance company, subject to the provisions of Title 18` TRUE

#ASSERT `s 145(h) the person stands in the same position with respect to the resulting or surviving corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(h) the person stands in the same position with respect to the resulting or surviving corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145(h) the person stands in the same position with respect to the resulting or surviving corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 145(i) the matter is within the reference` `an employee benefit plan, as an other enterprise` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(i) the matter is within the reference` `an excise tax assessed on a person with respect to an employee benefit plan, as a fine` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(i) the matter is within the reference` `service as a director, officer, employee or agent of the corporation which imposes duties on, or involves services by, the person with respect to an employee benefit plan, its participants or beneficiaries, as serving at the request of the corporation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(i) the matter is within the reference` `anything else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145(i) the person is deemed to have acted in a manner not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 145(i) the person is deemed to have acted in a manner not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 145(i) the person is deemed to have acted in a manner not opposed to the best interests of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
